msgid "Hierarchy uses tab for levels"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:319
msgid "When the hierarchy uses tab, the Tab key types a tab. To leave the field with the keyboard, press Escape and then Tab, or press Shift+Tab. Alternatively, use the space option and type a space for each level."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:374
msgid "This tool allows you to import terms into an existing taxonomy."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:375
msgid "The terms entered are not linked to any posts by this process."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:376
msgid "As only the term name is entered, its slug is be derived from that and no description is created. These can be edited using standard WordPress functionality if required"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:377
msgid "Usage"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:379
msgid "The simplest option is to enter a list of terms where each one is its name. Its slug will be generated automatically."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:380
msgid "This is entered as a list with no hierarchy. It is appropriate for either non-hierarchical taxonomies or a few entries of a hierarchical one."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:381
msgid "You can also enter entries hierarchically into a hierarchical taxonomy. For this, you need to indent the entries to identify the hierarchy of terms wanted."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:382
msgid "When the hierarchy uses tab, the Tab key types a tab in the list. To leave the list with the keyboard, press Escape and then Tab, or press Shift+Tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:383
msgid "In particular, you may want to add terms into an existing hierarchy. So to identify where the entries are to go, you need to enter the existing term (either name or slug) in the list with no indent - and then to follow it by the sub-tree of terms to be added."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:384
msgid "An implication of this is that it tries to identify if the term entered already exists and does not try to enter it again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:385
msgid "Thus the count of terms added displayed will not be the number of lines present."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:386
msgid "Terms migrate"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-simpletaxonomyrefreshed-admin-import.php:387
msgid "The migrate tool allows you to copy existing terms of a taxonomy to pre-populate this screen for populating a taxonomy."
msgstr ""

